{%- if aiFeedback %}
<style>{% include "css/message-box.css" %}</style>
<style>{% include "css/copy-feedback.css" %}</style>
<aside class="message-box ai-feedback" aria-labelledby="ai-feedback-title">
	<h2 id="ai-feedback-title">AI copy feedback</h2>

	{#- The nickname is named with its model on the same line, so nobody can read
	    "Penny Red" as a colleague of flesh and blood. `aiFeedback.model` is the model that
	    reviewed *this* post, not whatever the site collaborates with today. -#}
	<p>Copyedited with {{ metadata.collaborator.name }} — my {{ metadata.collaborator.roles.copy }}, which is {{ aiFeedback.model }} — on <time datetime="{{ aiFeedback.reviewed | htmlDateString }}">{{ aiFeedback.reviewed | readableDate }}</time>. Each change names the rule behind it, so you can check it yourself rather than taking an AI’s word for it.</p>

	<ol class="ai-feedback-list">
		{%- for change in aiFeedback.changes %}
		<li>
			<details>
				{#- The diff carries its meaning in bold and strikethrough, and <del>/<ins> are
				    not announced by NVDA or VoiceOver, so read aloud the marked-up version is
				    the before and after run together into one unintelligible string. Hide the
				    visual form and state the change in words instead.

				    No `smartquotes` on these two: some corrections are *about* a quote mark,
				    and curling them here would announce a before that never existed. -#}
				<summary class="diff">
					<span aria-hidden="true">{{ change.before | inlineDiff(change.after) | safe }}</span>
					<span class="visually-hidden">Before: {{ change.before }}. After: {{ change.after }}.</span>
				</summary>
				<p>{{ change.why | smartquotes }}</p>
				<p class="ai-feedback-source">{{ change.source | smartquotes }}</p>
			</details>
		</li>
		{%- endfor %}
	</ol>

	<p class="ai-feedback-more"><a href="/copy-feedback/">Every correction across the site</a></p>
</aside>
{%- endif %}
